				<h1 class="nunito-sans-700 text-2xl text-slate-900 mb-1">Privacy Statement</h1>
				<p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mb-6">Direct Route Collections Limited · membershipassyst.co.uk · Version 1.2</p>

				<ol class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>In order to apply through Membership Assyst for a credit account with the person from whom you are seeking credit, we will need to obtain information about you. That information will be controlled by Direct Route Collections Limited trading as Membership Assyst ("<strong>Membership Assyst</strong>"). Membership Assyst takes its duties under the Data Protection Act ("<strong>the Act</strong>") very seriously. In order for us to be able to process your application, and provide services to you and the person from whom you are seeking a credit account, we need to have your consent to the following uses being made of any information we are provided with about you.</li>

					<li>If you have any queries, Membership Assyst can be contacted by writing to us at: <strong>Direct Route Collections Limited, membershipassyst.co.uk</strong>.</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Your Information</h2>
				<ol start="3" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>
						Membership Assyst may collect and store some or all of the information set out below ("<strong>Your Information</strong>"). We will obtain this information from you, the company from whom you are seeking a credit account and / or third parties (including, but not limited to, third party credit reference agencies). This information may include:
						<ol class="mt-2 space-y-2 list-[lower-alpha] list-outside pl-5">
							<li>your name, address and the contact details of the appropriate person(s) within your organisation;</li>
							<li>information of the types set out in a credit application request;</li>
							<li>whether or not the person from whom you are seeking a credit account has accepted, rejected, modified, left pending or taken any other steps whatsoever in relation to your request;</li>
							<li>the credit limit agreed between you and the person from whom you are seeking a credit account;</li>
							<li>information contained in any correspondence the person from whom you are seeking a credit account (or persons on their behalf) sends to us, to persons on behalf of whom we are acting, to our data contributors, to persons who may be contacted via us, or to you via (or copied to) us. For the avoidance of doubt this may include (but is not limited to) allegations by the person from whom you are seeking a credit account, and/or by the person with whom you already hold a credit account, that you are in arrears for any sum or sums;</li>
							<li>information contained in any correspondence you (or persons acting on your behalf) send to us, to persons on behalf of whom we are acting, or to persons who may be contacted via us;</li>
							<li>information concerning you obtained from third party credit reference agencies;</li>
							<li>information concerning you obtained from Powers Limited trading as the Register of Outstanding Invoices ("<strong>ROSI</strong>"), as to which see paragraphs 10–13 below;</li>
							<li>information concerning you lawfully obtained from any other third parties;</li>
							<li>any information as we are required to collect and / or store under any enactment law or pursuant to an order or decision of any Court which has (or in our sole discretion arguably has) jurisdiction over us;</li>
							<li>any other information that we in our sole discretion feel to be necessary, expedient, convenient or useful to record about you.</li>
						</ol>
					</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Use of Your Information</h2>
				<ol start="4" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>
						Your Information will be kept, accessed, analysed, used and passed on by us for the following purposes:
						<ol class="mt-2 space-y-2 list-[lower-alpha] list-outside pl-5">
							<li>passing on Your Information, or so much of it as seems appropriate to us in the circumstances, to the person from whom you are seeking a credit account or to the person with whom you already hold a credit account so that they can assess whether or not, and if so to what extent, to extend you credit or continue to extend credit to you;</li>
							<li>passing on Your Information as contained in or relating to any other correspondence from you (or persons acting on your behalf), or so much of it as seems appropriate to us in the circumstances, to the person from whom you are seeking a credit account so that they can be made aware of and / or deal with such matters as are raised in that correspondence;</li>
							<li>so that we, on behalf of the person from whom you are seeking a credit account, can monitor the number, nature, total or individual exposure, or any other aspect of the credit accounts applied for, accepted, rejected or under consideration by that person or of business in general or of any particular section of business;</li>
							<li>so that we can pass on Your Information to the person from whom you are seeking a credit account so that they may monitor any aspect of the credit accounts applied for, accepted, rejected or under consideration by that person;</li>
							<li>so that we, on our own behalf, can monitor the number, nature, total or individual exposure, or any other aspect of the credit accounts applied for, accepted, rejected or under consideration by our clients or any of them;</li>
							<li>so that we can perform credit checks upon you. Such credit checks may be performed at about the time you apply for a credit account, as well as from time to time thereafter;</li>
							<li>so that we can select and supply Your Information to third party credit reference agencies, for performing credit checks upon you;</li>
							<li>so that we can perform checks to see whether you appear in ROSI;</li>
							<li>so that, in the event that it is alleged by the person from whom you are seeking a credit account that you are in arrears for any sum or sums, then Your Information (including the nature and extent of the debt), or so much of it as seems appropriate, may be passed to any third party credit reference agencies and / or entered into ROSI;</li>
							<li>so that we can record and / or fulfil any correspondence sent by you (or persons on your behalf) to us;</li>
							<li>so that we can record any correspondence sent by us to you (or persons on your behalf);</li>
							<li>so that we can communicate with you, both generally and in relation to any specific topics, issues, products, goods and / or services that we, or selected third parties, may from time to time offer;</li>
							<li>so that we can record and / or fulfil any requests by you of us for any products, goods and / or services that we, or selected third parties, may from time to time offer;</li>
							<li>so that we can pass on Your Information to our current or future business partners so that they may use your data to assess, analyse, and make decisions based upon your identity, creditworthiness, past trading history, business reliability, and general business status and history. In particular, our current or future business partners may include: Banks, Building Societies, Credit Reference Agencies, Debt Insurance Companies, Debt Collection Agencies, Factoring/Invoice Discounting Companies, Credit Card Companies, Insolvency Practitioners, Merger and/or Acquisition companies, Financial Stockbrokers, Solicitors, and Trade Associations;</li>
							<li>such other uses as we in our sole discretion feel to be necessary, expedient, convenient or useful;</li>
							<li>as required under any enactment law or pursuant to an order or decision of any Court which has (or in our sole discretion arguably has) jurisdiction over us.</li>
						</ol>
					</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Consent to the Supply of Your Data</h2>
				<ol start="5" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>By agreeing to this Privacy Statement you also agree to the person from whom you are seeking a credit account providing us with such of Your Data as is within their possession for the purposes set out in this Privacy Statement. For the purpose of obtaining this consent Membership Assyst is acting as the agent of the person from whom you are seeking a credit account.</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Historical Information</h2>
				<ol start="6" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>Your Information will be stored by us for so long as your account is live and for a period of not more than 6 years thereafter.</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Modification of Your Information</h2>
				<ol start="7" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>If you wish to modify or update any of Your Information, please use the website. If you need help, please contact us at the address given above.</li>
					<li>In the event that you dispute the correctness of any of Your Information, please contact us at the address given above, and we will either amend our records to correct that information or, in our sole discretion, amend it to indicate that you dispute that aspect and record a summary of why you take this view.</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Transfer of Business</h2>
				<ol start="9" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>In the event that the whole or part of our business is sold to any other undertaking, you agree that Your Information (insofar as relevant to that part of the business so sold) can be transferred to that person, and used by them under the terms of this Privacy Policy.</li>
				</ol>

				<h2 class="nunito-sans-700 text-base text-slate-800 mt-7 mb-3">Agreement to the ROSI Register Process</h2>
				<ol start="10" class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-outside pl-5">
					<li>Where we refer to ROSI in this Privacy Statement, we mean the Register of Outstanding Invoices, and any branded versions thereof. Full details of ROSI can be found at <a href="http://www.outstandinginvoices.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[#1e3a8a] underline">www.outstandinginvoices.com</a>.</li>
					<li>As mentioned in paragraph 3 above, in order to supply the services we offer to the person from whom you are seeking a credit account, we may need to pass your information to ROSI in order to check your credit status and / or whether there are any entries against your name under ROSI.</li>
					<li>In addition we strongly believe that our clients and those seeking credit from them should behave with the highest of commercial integrity. To that end, in order for us to be willing to process your application / provide our services to the person from whom you are seeking credit, we require you to agree to be subject to the ROSI process in general.</li>
					<li>
						As such, by agreeing to this Privacy Policy you agree to us or any third party transferring to Powers Limited or any successor in title thereto, and to Powers Limited recording, storing, analysing, publicising and / or using certain data:
						<ol class="mt-2 space-y-2 list-[lower-alpha] list-outside pl-5">
							<li>for the purposes of the ROSI process and / or the ROSI register;</li>
							<li>for monitoring the number, nature, status, total or individual exposure of the entries under the ROSI register;</li>
							<li>for otherwise monitoring, analysing or controlling any aspect of the ROSI business;</li>
							<li>for communicating with you or any other person in relation to the ROSI process and / or the ROSI register; and / or</li>
							<li>for publicising that data, and / or the debt related thereto, on the ROSI register.</li>
						</ol>
					</li>
				</ol>

